# 7. CASE WHEN

### SQL

```sql
SELECT
    customer_id,
    CASE
        WHEN total_spend > 10000 THEN 'High'
        WHEN total_spend > 5000 THEN 'Medium'
        ELSE 'Low'
    END AS customer_segment
FROM customers;
```

### PySpark

```python
df = df.withColumn(
    "customer_segment",
    F.when(F.col("total_spend") > 10000, "High")
     .when(F.col("total_spend") > 5000, "Medium")
     .otherwise("Low")
)
```

### Quick Mapping

| SQL         | PySpark        |
| ----------- | -------------- |
| `CASE WHEN` | `F.when()`     |
| `ELSE`      | `.otherwise()` |

