# 9. Date Functions

| Requirement          | SQL                          | PySpark                        |
| -------------------- | ---------------------------- | ------------------------------ |
| Current date         | `GETDATE()` / `CURRENT_DATE` | `F.current_date()`             |
| Current timestamp    | `GETDATE()`                  | `F.current_timestamp()`        |
| Add days             | `DATEADD(DAY, 7, date)`      | `F.date_add("date", 7)`        |
| Subtract days        | `DATEADD(DAY, -7, date)`     | `F.date_sub("date", 7)`        |
| Difference           | `DATEDIFF(end, start)`       | `F.datediff("end", "start")`   |
| Extract year         | `YEAR(date)`                 | `F.year("date")`               |
| Extract month        | `MONTH(date)`                | `F.month("date")`              |
| Extract day          | `DAY(date)`                  | `F.day("date")`                |
| Format date          | `FORMAT(date, ...)`          | `F.date_format("date", "...")` |
| Convert to date      | `CAST(date AS DATE)`         | `F.to_date("date")`            |
| Convert to timestamp | `CAST(date AS TIMESTAMP)`    | `F.to_timestamp("date")`       |

### Example

```python
df = df.withColumn(
    "days_since_policy_start",
    F.datediff(
        F.current_date(),
        F.col("policy_start_date")
    )
)
```

