# 10. Joins

| SQL          | PySpark                          |
| ------------ | -------------------------------- |
| `INNER JOIN` | `.join(df2, condition, "inner")` |
| `LEFT JOIN`  | `.join(df2, condition, "left")`  |
| `RIGHT JOIN` | `.join(df2, condition, "right")` |
| `FULL JOIN`  | `.join(df2, condition, "full")   |
| `CROSS JOIN` | `.crossJoin(df2)`                |

### SQL

```sql
SELECT
    c.customer_id,
    c.name,
    o.order_id,
    o.amount
FROM customers c
INNER JOIN orders o
    ON c.customer_id = o.customer_id;
```

### PySpark

```python
result = customers.join(
    orders,
    customers.customer_id == orders.customer_id,
    "inner"
).select(
    customers.customer_id,
    customers.name,
    orders.order_id,
    orders.amount
)
```

