# 22. Repartition vs Coalesce

| Requirement                  | PySpark                         |
| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------- |
| Increase/decrease partitions | `df.repartition(10)`            |
| Repartition by column        | `df.repartition("customer_id")` |
| Reduce partitions            | `df.coalesce(5)`                |

### Example

```python
df = df.repartition(
    10,
    "customer_id"
)
```

> `repartition()` causes a shuffle.
> `coalesce()` is generally useful when reducing partitions without a full shuffle.

