# 23. Cache vs Persist

| SQL Concept            | PySpark          |
| ---------------------- | ---------------- |
| No direct equivalent   | `df.cache()`     |
| Persist in memory/disk | `df.persist()`   |
| Remove cache           | `df.unpersist()` |

### Example

```python
df.cache()

df.count()

# Reuse df several times

df.unpersist()
```

> Cache only when the DataFrame is reused and recomputation would be expensive.

