# 26. SQL → PySpark Complete Example

### SQL

```sql
SELECT
    region,
    COUNT(*) AS total_orders,
    SUM(quantity * unit_price) AS total_sales,
    AVG(quantity * unit_price) AS avg_order_value
FROM orders
WHERE order_date >= DATEADD(DAY, -30, GETDATE())
GROUP BY region
HAVING SUM(quantity * unit_price) > 10000
ORDER BY total_sales DESC;
```

### PySpark

```python
from pyspark.sql import functions as F

result = (
    orders
    .filter(
        F.col("order_date") >=
        F.date_sub(F.current_date(), 30)
    )
    .groupBy("region")
    .agg(
        F.count("*").alias("total_orders"),
        F.sum(
            F.col("quantity") *
            F.col("unit_price")
        ).alias("total_sales"),
        F.avg(
            F.col("quantity") *
            F.col("unit_price")
        ).alias("avg_order_value")
    )
    .filter(
        F.col("total_sales") > 10000
    )
    .orderBy(
        F.col("total_sales").desc()
    )
)
```

