## The PySpark Mental Model

As a SQL developer, remember:

```text
SQL                         PySpark

TABLE                  →    DataFrame
SELECT                 →    select()
WHERE                  →    filter()
GROUP BY               →    groupBy()
HAVING                 →    filter() after aggregation
JOIN                   →    join()
ORDER BY               →    orderBy()
CASE WHEN              →    when().otherwise()
WINDOW FUNCTION        →    Window + over()
INSERT/CREATE TABLE    →    write()
SQL execution          →    Spark execution plan
```

### The most common PySpark pattern

```python
result = (
    df
    .filter(...)
    .withColumn(...)
    .select(...)
    .groupBy(...)
    .agg(...)
    .join(...)
    .orderBy(...)
)
```

**Think of PySpark as SQL expressed as a chain of DataFrame transformations.**
